/-!
# Cyclic N-isogeny of lattice curves comes from index-N sublattice

Theorem statement:
`PeriodPair.exists_scale_lattice_subset_and_sublatticeIndex_eq_and_isAddCyclic_sublatticeQuotient`
(`aa8de0ab-6fe5-5b54-9c67-7eb99189b746`), by Claude, 2026-09-05.

Proof: submission `c1ce856c-80f9-5744-ba79-9be9c873e49a`, by Claude, 2026-09-05 (ACCEPTED); locally
adapted.

Let $L$ and $L'$ be period pairs, with associated Weierstrass curves $y^2 = x^3 - (g_2/4)x - g_3/4$
over $\mathbb{C}$ formed from their Eisenstein invariants, and assume both curves are elliptic and
both affine curves satisfy: `GenusOnePlaceGate`, i.e. a bijection between the points of the curve
and the places of its function field over $\mathbb{C}$, all of degree $1$;
`GenusOnePlaceGate.IsCentred`, i.e. for every nonsingular pair $(x,y)$ the images in the function
field of the coordinate-ring classes of $X$ and of $Y - y$ lie in the nonunits of the valuation
subring of the place attached to the point $(x,y)$; and `AbelTheorem`, i.e. a divisor of degree $0$
is principal exactly when its divisor sum vanishes. Let $\iota$ be a $\mathbb{C}$-algebra
homomorphism from the function field of the $L'$-curve to that of the $L$-curve, assumed integral as
a ring homomorphism, assumed finite in the sense that the target is a finite module over the source
along $\iota$ (`hfin`), and satisfying the pushforward norm formula for divisors along $\iota$
(`hN`). Let $N$ be a nonzero natural number, and suppose the kernel of `pointMapOfPushforward ι hι
hfin hN`, the additive homomorphism from the points of the $L$-curve to the points of the $L'$-curve
obtained by transporting the pushforward map on degree-zero divisor classes through the two
point–$\mathrm{Pic}^0$ identifications, is cyclic of cardinality $N$. Then there is a unit $\beta
\in \mathbb{C}^\times$ such that the lattice of $L'.\mathrm{scale}\,\beta$, namely $\beta\Lambda'$
generated by $\beta\omega_1'$ and $\beta\omega_2'$, is contained in the lattice $\Lambda$ of $L$,
the index of $\beta\Lambda'$ as a subgroup of $\Lambda$ equals $N$, and the quotient
$\Lambda/\beta\Lambda'$ is cyclic.

This is the analytic dictionary for isogenies of complex elliptic curves: a cyclic $N$-isogeny
between two lattice curves is realised, after rescaling the target lattice, by an inclusion of
lattices of index $N$ with cyclic quotient. It is used in the passage from a cyclic $N$-isogeny to a
relation between the $j$-invariants of the two curves, as in
[`WeierstrassCurve.Affine.
eval_modularPolynomial_map_j_eq_zero_of_isAddCyclic_ker_pointMapOfPushforward`]
(thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.Affine.
eval_modularPolynomial_map_j_eq_zero_of_isAddCyclic_ker_pointMapOfPushforward)
and
[`WeierstrassCurve.Affine.IsogenyEndDatum.aeval_j_diag_eq_zero_of_finrankAlong_eq`]
(thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.Affine.IsogenyEndDatum.aeval_j_diag_eq_zero_of_finrankAlong_eq).

